	(text "From LED datasheet the Typical Voltage drop at 5 mA is 2.95V.\nKnowing this, I can compute the series resistor:\n	R = (3.3V - V_forw_LED) / 5 mA = 70 Ohm\n	--> E12 series (5% Toll.), R = 82 Ohm\n\nIf the Actual Forward Voltage of the LED is higher, it will simply light up with\nlower luminosity, so using the typical Forward Voltage value is ok (I don't need to \nbe precise on the actual current flowing in the LED, I just need it to light up)"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 52.832 241.808 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 0.762 0.762)
			)
			(justify left)
		)
		(uuid "0da14fe0-e786-4a7a-90c3-23363d84f856")
	)
	(text "\"Fault Simulation Connector\", which just disconnects\none of the Sensor outputs. Stuck-Open and \nStuck-to-GND faults can be simulated by this \nconnector"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 93.98 48.26 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 0.762 0.762)
			)
			(justify left)
		)
		(uuid "10e8b3b3-f23e-4abe-99f8-c651963ac37f")
	)
	(text "1st Order Filter"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 39.37 77.47 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
		)
		(uuid "163dab1d-8a43-4d06-9eac-7520fc1d233f")
	)
	(text "Differential Amplifier"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 262.636 14.986 0)
